    "updated_at": "2022-03-04T08:54:12Z",
    "body": "Actually there's something missing here I believe... the iframe and the embedder might have a different `cross-origin isolated capability`, so the timing might need to be coarsened if the embedder is stricter than the frame. The same will be needed for early hints, as the timestamps are marked before the document is created.\r\n\r\nI wonder if entries should be coarsened again when accessed (inside the `Resource Timing` spec) - which is what implementations do - it makes sure that the global object for coarsening is the one relevant to the entry regardless of how it was created.\r\n\r\n@annevk WDYT?",
    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
